# OPTIONAL subset of `inputs/apt-packages/base`.
#
# Interactive conveniences that no build step and no profile behaviour depends
# on. They are installed in the SAME single apt transaction as the required
# packages (the union list is unchanged, so layer bytes and dependency
# resolution stay identical for all 67 profiles), but their absence must NOT
# fail a build: if one becomes unavailable on an arch, it belongs here and
# nothing asserts it.
#
# Deliberately absent from features/system-essentials/feature.json's
# postInstallCheck for the same reason.
#
# Promotion rule: move a name to base.required only when something actually
# depends on it, and extend the postInstallCheck with its binary then.
fzf
tmux
neovim
